FUNCTION:    countAtRisk
MODULE:      grading
RESPONSIBLE FOR:  Prints the amount of students in the class are at risk

  PRE: Student Index > 0 and <= number of students - 1
       isAtRisk is true
  POST: Returns the number of students that are at risk
  SIDE EFFECTS: NONE
  RETURNS: The integer of students that are at risk

  PARAMETERS:
    name : style  — because (which contract line?)
    isAtRisk: boolean
    studentIndex: value
    scores: const &

  SIGNATURE: int countAtRisk(const ScoresGrid& scores);

  HARD TO TEST BECAUSE: You have to check the output

  TESTS:

  Correctly finds the number at risk with multiple students
  Correctly determines if a student is at risk with 1 student
  Correctly returns 0 when no students are at risk
  

FUNCTION:    findClassExtremes
MODULE:      grading
RESPONSIBLE FOR: Looks through scores in grid and find the lowest and highest along with the student row

  PRE: Assignment count is greater 0
  POST: Finds the highest, lowest and the student index
  SIDE EFFECTS: NONE
  RETURNS: Lowest, highest and student row it came from

  PARAMETERS:
    name : style  — because (which contract line?)
    scores: const & - the scores grid is not modified
    studentIndex: value

  SIGNATURE: void findClassExtremes(const ScoreGrid& scores, double& lowest, double& highest, int& lowestStudent, int& highestStudent);

  HARD TO TEST BECAUSE: n/a

  TEST:
  Correctly finds class extremes when there is 1 student
  Correctly finds class extremes when there are multiple students
  Correctly finds class extremes when multiple students have the same highest/lowest
  

FUNCTION:    applyCurve
MODULE:      grading
RESPONSIBLE FOR:  Adds 5 to student grades less than 100

  PRE: Student average is less than 100
  POST: Changes studentAverage by a set amount with a max cap of 100
  SIDE EFFECTS: Modifies studentAverage
  RETURNS: NONE

  PARAMETERS:
    name : style  — because (which contract line?)
    scores : const & the score grid is not modified
    studentIndex: value

  SIGNATURE: void applyCurve(const ScoreGrid& scores);

  HARD TO TEST BECAUSE: You have to check the gradebook and see if the result has changed

  TEST:
  Resulting grades are not greater than 100
  Applies curve correctly when there is 1 assignment
  Applies curve correctly when there is 1 student
  Applies curve correctly when there are multiple students
  Applies curve correctly when there are multiple assignments
  

FUNCTION:    topStudent
MODULE:      grading
RESPONSIBLE FOR: Checking which student has the highest student average

  PRE: Has to be the highest student average
  POST: Returns the row index of that student
  SIDE EFFECTS: NONE
  RETURNS: The row where the student has the highest grade

  PARAMETERS:
    name : style  — because (which contract line?)
    scores : const & the score grid is not modified
    studentIndex: value

  SIGNATURE: int topStudent(const ScoreGrid& scores);

  HARD TO TEST BECAUSE: You have to rely on output and logic to figure out the error

  TEST:
  Returns the first student when two students have the same average
  Returns index 0 when there is only 1 student
  Returns the correct student when there are multiple students
